abstract: "Every decision made by ten frontier AI models (one per company) acting as managers in a shared 13-round fantasy basketball snake draft held in October 2026, at the start of the NBA 2026-27 regular season, with web research, under fixed scoring rules (ESPN-standard points). Only games tipping off after the final pick are scored. Per-decision records give model identity, timing, research counts, source domains, token usage, estimated cost, failures and the selected player; per-call records give each model request and tool call. Optional companion files hold each AI's sealed pre-draft forecasts, a three-repeat consistency probe, and solo rosters built without competition. Outcomes are scored later against real games. One draft is descriptive, not a causal ranking of companies."
